    "statement": "The external evaluation suites are derived from distinct documented sources and share zero exact or normalized record collisions with the training corpus. However, because all web security benchmarks evaluate shared vulnerability archetypes (such as traversal sequences and SQL syntax), domain-level semantic overlap exists by design, and claims of absolute semantic independence are methodologically unsupportable.",
